Do not let an inline accessor hide the instance it reads

An inline method which reads a protected or private member does so through
an accessor the inliner makes (`inline$cells`). Where the member is an array,
the accessor's result type is `Array[T]^{any.rd}`, and since scala/scala3
#27524 separation checking took that for a definition hiding the enclosing
instance: every later access to `this` in the class was an error,

    Separation failure: Illegal access to {Parser.this} which is hidden by
    the previous definition of method zephyrine$Cursor$Snapshot$$inline$cells

which no annotation in the source can prevent, the accessor being the
compiler's. An inline accessor stands for a selection of the member, which
hides nothing where it is written out, and is no longer checked or recorded
as a definition.

Found in Soundness's ypsiloid, a parser extending the inline trait
zephyrine.Cursor.Snapshot.

